@mad@madbanana22 I suppose I should specify “realign”. The word “recenter” was misleading.

It takes a baseline center based on the fov of the camera. And it can tell where you are in relation to that center using the camera looking for the lights. It still uses these sensors shown in the video for its main function, but relies off this simple system to prevent the issue shown.

More so to handle rotation rather than position, but it does play a role for both.

